      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-141144",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4d48e2a0-1a76-5eec-a98c-4a7eb16f70cb",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying Multiplicity of a Root Given a Graph",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/4092c0852a573a0add69c6fb7b55f393d0767a5b6a2282a10194ea27cb1be9c4.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements is true?",
        "worked_solution": "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932088/assets/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=6.$ So, $x=6$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=6.$ So, $x=6$ has *even* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=6$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity.",
