        "knowledge_point_id": "f7614a05-f221-5fda-b491-6893f44a1a5f",
        "knowledge_point": "Dividing Rational Expressions with Multiple Common Factors",
        "problem": "Given that $\\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}=a$ and $\\frac{z-2}{6(z+1)}=b,$ what is $a÷b?$",
        "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\na÷b=\\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}÷\\frac{z-2}{6(z+1)},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}÷\\frac{z-2}{6(z+1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(z-2)}{(z+1)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{6(z+1)}{z-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\cancel{(z-2)}}{(z+1)^{\\cancel{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{6\\cancel{(z+1)}}{\\cancel{(z-2)}} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{z+1}\\cdot 6 & = \\\\ \\frac{18}{z+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
